<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93865" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σηρῐκός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σήρ</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Seric, silken</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσθής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Salt.</u>
					63
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπετάσματα, σκευή</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				43.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				59.26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					10.942
				</span></i>
			 (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				2.31
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ς. τῶν ὑφασμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.396b
				</span></i>
			; written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρικός</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				5.46
			</span></i>:—as Subst., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σηρικόν</span></b> , τό,
				<i>silken robe, silk,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Apoc.
				18.12
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιρικόν</span>
			), <i>Peripl.M. Rubr.</i><i><span class="en">
				49
			</span></i>; in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Nearch.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				15.1.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σηρικά, τά</span>, <i>jujubes</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.614
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				1.81
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σηρικόν</span> (fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συρικόν</span>), τό, a
				<i>red pigment</i>, Olymp.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.76
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Zos.Alch.
				p.248
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>; <i>Syricum pigmentum, quod Syrii Phoenices in Rubri maris
				litoribus colligunt</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isid.
				<u>Etym.</u>
				19.17.6
			</span></i> (where it is distd. from <u>Sericum</u>).</div>
